# Manual API calls, grown episode by episode.
# Run with IntelliJ HTTP Client or the VS Code "REST Client" extension
# against a running app: ./mvnw spring-boot:run, or since Episode 19 docker compose --profile app up --build
#
# Since Episode 10 every POST /payments needs an Idempotency-Key. Re-running a request
# with the same key returns the payment it created the first time; change the key
# to create a new one.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Episode 01 — create payment -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-01-request-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-20001",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "Invoice 12345"
}

### Episode 01 — unsupported currency -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-01-request-2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-20001",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "currency": "JPY",
  "reference": "Invoice 12345"
}

### Episode 01 — same source and destination -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-01-request-3
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "Invoice 12345"
}

### Episode 01 — non-positive amount -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-01-request-4
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-20001",
  "amount": 0,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "Invoice 12345"
}

### Episode 03 — unknown source account -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-03-request-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-99999",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-20001",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "Invoice 12345"
}

### Episode 03 — closed destination account -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-03-request-2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-90001",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "Invoice 12345"
}

### Episode 05 — create a payment to read back -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-05-request-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-30001",
  "amount": 99.95,
  "currency": "GBP",
  "reference": "Rent October"
}

### Episode 05 — read it back -> 200 (paste the paymentId from the response above)
@paymentId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
GET {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{paymentId}}

### Episode 05 — unknown payment -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/payments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Episode 05 — malformed payment id -> 400 "Invalid payment id"
GET {{baseUrl}}/payments/not-a-uuid

### Episode 06 — amount exactly at the limit -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-06-request-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-20001",
  "amount": 10000.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "Invoice 12345"
}

### Episode 06 — amount over the limit -> 400 "Payment amount must not exceed 10000.00 EUR" (since Episode 12: 201, the limit is checked on execute)
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-06-request-2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-20001",
  "amount": 10000.01,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "Invoice 12345"
}

### Episode 07 — frozen account in the external account system -> 400 "is not active"
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-07-request-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-80001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-20001",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "Invoice 12345"
}

### Episode 07 — ask the fake account system directly (WireMock from docker-compose.yml)
GET http://localhost:8089/accounts/ACC-80001

### Episode 08 — unknown payment -> 404 problem details "Payment ... does not exist"
GET {{baseUrl}}/payments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Episode 08 — missing fields -> 400 problem details, same shape as our own errors
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-08-request-1
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Episode 08 — account system down -> 503 "Account system is unavailable"
# First run: docker compose stop account-system   (afterwards: docker compose start account-system)
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-08-request-2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-20001",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "Invoice 12345"
}

### Episode 09 — create a payment to execute -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-09-request-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-20001",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "Invoice 12345"
}

### Episode 09 — execute it -> 200 "COMPLETED" (since Episode 17: 202 "CREATED", then GET shows COMPLETED) (paste the paymentId from the response above)
@executePaymentId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{executePaymentId}}/execute

### Episode 09 — execute it again -> 409 "is COMPLETED and cannot become PROCESSING"
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{executePaymentId}}/execute

### Episode 09 — a payment the stub payment system rejects -> 201, then execute it -> 200 "FAILED" (since Episode 17: 202, then GET shows FAILED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-09-request-2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-20001",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "REJECT insufficient funds"
}

