POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-10-demo-key-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-20001",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "Invoice 10010"
}

### Episode 10 — same key, same request -> 201 with the same paymentId, no second payment
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-10-demo-key-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-20001",
  "amount": 250,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "Invoice 10010"
}

### Episode 10 — same key, different amount -> 422 "already used for a different request"
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-10-demo-key-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-20001",
  "amount": 999.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "Invoice 10010"
}

### Episode 10 — no Idempotency-Key -> 400 "Required header 'Idempotency-Key' is not present."
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-20001",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "Invoice 10011"
}

### Episode 11 — create a payment to cancel -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-11-demo-key-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-20001",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "Invoice 11011"
}

### Episode 11 — cancel it -> 200 "CANCELLED" (paste the paymentId from the response above)
@cancelPaymentId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{cancelPaymentId}}/cancel

### Episode 11 — execute the cancelled payment -> 409 "is CANCELLED and cannot become PROCESSING"
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{cancelPaymentId}}/execute

### Episode 11 — cancel the COMPLETED payment from Episode 09 -> 409 "is COMPLETED and cannot become CANCELLED"
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{executePaymentId}}/cancel

### Episode 12 — a payment to an account the authorization system declines -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-12-demo-key-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-70001",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "Invoice 12012"
}

### Episode 12 — execute it -> 422 "was not authorized", payment stays CREATED (since Episode 17: 202, the decline is only in the log; GET still shows CREATED) (paste the paymentId above)
@declinedPaymentId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{declinedPaymentId}}/execute

### Episode 12 — a payment over the source account's limit -> 201 (limits are checked on execute)
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-12-demo-key-2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-20001",
  "amount": 10000.01,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "Invoice 12013"
}

### Episode 12 — execute it -> 422 "exceeds the source account's limit", payment is now AUTHORIZED (since Episode 17: 202, then GET shows AUTHORIZED) (paste the paymentId above)
@overLimitPaymentId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{overLimitPaymentId}}/execute

### Episode 13 — create a payment to follow through the audit trail -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-13-demo-key-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-20001",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "Invoice 13013"
}

### Episode 13 — execute it -> 200 COMPLETED (since Episode 17: 202, then COMPLETED); three rows in payment_audit (see docs/episodes/13) (paste the paymentId above)
@auditedPaymentId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{auditedPaymentId}}/execute

### Episode 15 — create with your own correlation ID -> 201, X-Correlation-Id: episode-15-demo in the response and in every log line
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-15-demo-key-1
X-Correlation-Id: episode-15-demo
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-20001",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "Invoice 15015"
}

### Episode 15 — the metrics Prometheus scrapes (look for payments_total, payment_execution_duration_seconds)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/prometheus

### Episode 16 — create a payment the payment system settles, but answers too late -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-16-demo-key-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-20001",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "TIMEOUT Invoice 16016"
}

### Episode 16 — execute it -> after 5s, 200 with "status": "PROCESSING" (outcome unknown); again -> 409 (since Episode 17: 202 at once; GET shows PROCESSING) (paste the paymentId above)
@unknownOutcomePaymentId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{unknownOutcomePaymentId}}/execute

### Episode 16 — circuit breaker states (after `docker compose stop account-system` and a few creates, account-system is open)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/prometheus

### Episode 17 — create a payment to execute asynchronously -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Idempotency-Key: episode-17-demo-key-1
X-Correlation-Id: episode-17-demo
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-10001",
  "destinationAccountId": "ACC-20001",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "Invoice 17017"
}

### Episode 17 — execute it -> 202 with "status": "CREATED": queued, not done yet (paste the paymentId above)
@asyncPaymentId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{asyncPaymentId}}/execute
X-Correlation-Id: episode-17-demo

### Episode 17 — follow it -> 200 "COMPLETED" a moment later; the consumer's log lines carry correlationId episode-17-demo
GET {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{asyncPaymentId}}

### Episode 17 — execute it again -> 409 "is COMPLETED and cannot become PROCESSING", nothing is queued
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{asyncPaymentId}}/execute

### Episode 17 — broker down (`docker compose stop kafka`): execute a payment that is still CREATED -> 503 "Message broker is unavailable" after 2s
@brokerDownPaymentId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{brokerDownPaymentId}}/execute
